# Copy to .env and fill in the two secrets. .env is gitignored — never commit a filled copy.
#
# You do not have to edit this by hand. Ask your agent to do it:
#   "save my Molecule credential: mol_…"     -> writes MOLECULE_CONSUMER_CREDENTIAL
#   "create your wallet"                     -> writes MOLECULE_AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY
# It creates the file at mode 0600 and replaces a line rather than duplicating it.
#
# Three things that trip people up:
#   * On macOS a .env is hidden in Finder — press Cmd+Shift+. to show hidden files.
#   * The MCP server reads this once at startup. After editing, reconnect it (/mcp in
#     Claude Code) or the change will look like it did nothing.
#   * A real environment variable WINS over this file. If a value here seems to be
#     ignored, check whether something already exports it (a shell profile, or a
#     .claude/settings.json env block in a parent directory).

# --- the two you need ---

# Your Molecule API credential. Think of it as an API key: it identifies whose calls these
# are and can be revoked. It is NOT a wallet and holds no funds.
# Webinar/starter-pack users: it is in your starter pack. Otherwise ask the Molecule team
# on Discord — there is no self-serve page.
MOLECULE_CONSUMER_CREDENTIAL=

# The agent's own wallet key, created once by the agent and kept here. A new key is a
# DIFFERENT agent with no role on your Lab, and you would have to grant the role again.
# This is the agent's key, never yours, and it needs no funds.
MOLECULE_AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- optional ---

# The agent's write token. It issues one whenever it needs one, so this is only worth
# setting to save a later session from issuing another.
MOLECULE_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# --- overrides: leave these alone unless the Molecule team gives you values ---
#
# The defaults point at the live Labs API and there is nothing to configure here.
#
# These exist so the Molecule team can point an agent at another deployment. If you set
# ANY of them, set them as a MATCHED SET: the API, the chain id and the access resolver
# all have to describe the same deployment. Mixing them — a different API with the live
# chain and resolver, say — produces private files that upload cleanly and can then never
# be decrypted, because the lock names a contract that deployment cannot evaluate.
#
# MOLECULE_LABS_URL=
# MOLECULE_CLIENT_URL=
# MOLECULE_CHAIN_ID=
# MOLECULE_ACCESS_RESOLVER=

# Read-only chain endpoint, used to check a private file's lock before encrypting. Defaults
# to a public node for whichever chain is configured; set this to use a dedicated one if
# the public node rate-limits you.
# EVM_RPC_URL=
